  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening a Climate Smart, Green, and Resilient Education System i</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rising global temperatures lead to more frequent climate-related disasters in vulnerable countries like Nepal, despite low emission rates, increasing &quot;learning poverty&quot; up to 90%. In response, this project titled &quot;Strengthening a Climate Smart, Green and Resilient Education System in Nepal&quot; will strengthen the curriculum to include climate change, train teachers in pedagogical methods and promote eco-friendly practices in &apos;green&apos; model schools. UNESCO and UNICEF will collaborate on a three-year project in Nepal, with UNESCO as the lead partner and UNICEF as the co-partner. The project will be funded by the Royal Norwegian Embassy in Nepal.</narrative>
  </description>
